From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:10:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SNDCHIP: start the counters and registers at 0

The constructor left the tone, noise and envelope counters, the noise
output, the chip type and the registers uninitialised (set_timings then
applied the registers it had not set): each voice's first period, and
the noise until its first period, came from whatever memory the chip was
built in, so two voices of one dump played differently. They now start
at 0.
---
 src/audiosource/ay/sndchip.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/ay/sndchip.cpp b/src/audiosource/ay/sndchip.cpp
index 4ae2300..6182997 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/ay/sndchip.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/ay/sndchip.cpp
@@ -204,6 +204,12 @@ SNDCHIP::SNDCHIP(SNDBUFFER& buffer)
                 : SNDRENDER(buffer)
 {
         bitA = bitB = bitC = 0;
+        // What set_timings and reset do not set, and the registers
+        // apply_regs reads.
+        ta = tb = tc = tn = te = 0;
+        bitN = 0;
+        chiptype = CHIP_YM;
+        memset(reg, 0, sizeof(reg));
         set_timings(SNDR_DEFAULT_SYSTICK_RATE, SNDR_DEFAULT_AY_RATE, SNDR_DEFAULT_SAMPLE_RATE);
         set_chip(CHIP_YM);
         set_volumes(0x7FFF, SNDR_VOL_YM, SNDR_PAN_ABC);
